Etch a radio button with the custom dark alpha

The upper etch arc of a radio button takes a fixed alpha. The lower arc
of the same block takes the custom light alpha, and the check box beside
it takes both custom values. The custom dark alpha therefore reaches no
part of the radio button, while the group states that the style always
uses the alpha values.

The upper arc now takes the custom dark alpha while the group holds
custom values. The two arcs of the etch follow the two spin boxes. A
configuration with no custom alphas keeps the fixed alpha and the paint
of before.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 20 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/style/qtcurve_primitive.cpp b/qt6/style/qtcurve_primitive.cpp
index 0b6b5053..c47d98ac 100644
--- a/qt6/style/qtcurve_primitive.cpp
+++ b/qt6/style/qtcurve_primitive.cpp
@@ -1619,7 +1619,9 @@ Style::drawPrimitiveIndicatorRadioButton(PrimitiveElement,
                 (glow || opts.buttonEffect != EFFECT_NONE || sunken)) {
                 QColor topCol = glow ? m_mouseOverCols[GLOW_MO] : Qt::black;
                 if (!glow) {
-                    topCol.setAlphaF(ETCH_RADIO_TOP_ALPHA);
+                    topCol.setAlphaF(USE_CUSTOM_ALPHAS(opts) ?
+                                     opts.customAlphas[ALPHA_ETCH_DARK] :
+                                     ETCH_RADIO_TOP_ALPHA);
                 }
                 setPainterPen(painter, topCol, QPENWIDTH1);
                 painter->drawArc(QRectF(x - 0.5, y - 0.5, opts.crSize + 1,
